{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/512617-the-resources-background-in-wraith-20th-anniversary","id":512617,"title":"The \"Resources\" Background in Wraith 20th Anniversary.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-12T23:12:13-07:00","id":512617,"title":"The \"Resources\" Background in Wraith 20th Anniversary.","content":"I've noticed that Wraith remains pretty much the ONLY Old Storyteller System RPG (Exalted Included) that does not have the &quot;Resources&quot; Background Option for its characters.<br /> <br /> Normally, one would be able to justify that by the fact that &quot;Mortal Wealth has no meaning to one who can't carry it over into the afterlife&quot; (Not so much an issue with Asian Ghosts, as Our Cultures regularly burns/sends Afterlife Money to Our Loved-Ones and Ancestors so they won't be poor there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> But then comes the issue of the Chests full of Obli Coins that an Wealthy and Politically Affluent Wraith would have in order to utilize his Wealth and Influence.<br /> <br /> So, I wonder: For Wraith 20 would there finally be a &quot;Resources&quot; Background that would address the amount of Obli your character owns, and the amount that enters your coffers through your daily job in the Hierarchy?<br /> <br /> For that matter, would there be a price-list/resource-cost list in the Equipment and Weapons section for the amount of Obli/Underworld Money needed to acquire Artefacts/Housing/Basic Clothes?<br /> <br /> Because to address the issue of Afterlife Money only to NOT have a system that involves how it is acquired and used is a bit contradictory, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Hopefully Wraith 20 will finally address this mystery! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T00:37:55-07:00","id":512698,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer: I never played wraith and only tried to run a game once. Content of this post is based on few experience and a lot of speculation. It may contain nuts as well.<br /> <br /> Iirc Oboli are forged from soulsteel or if you're lucky enough are relics from your grave.<br /> So why not buy them with the relic and/or artifact backgrounds?<br /> <br /> A house also is only solid if its a relic or artifact so if you own it. Take one of these backgrounds (maybe haunt qualifies as well).<br /> <br /> Clothing should be formed by the subconsciousness of the psyche as its part of the wraiths appearance imho.<br /> <br /> However. If your character didn't fake his death but instead fakes to be still alive by manipulating his computer and some of the living to reaolve his passions. Then the original ressources background might come in handy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T00:44:27-07:00","id":512704,"title":"","content":"Oh. And if the house you &quot;live&quot; in comes with a job in the hierarchy, I'd suggest to take some &quot;status&quot; background to reflect the privilege to have a home you didn't have to buy. If you loose your job in the hierarchy, you loose these privileges as well (you don't hope for reaching the &quot;retirement age&quot; of a wraith... at least I hope so xD )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T10:11:09-07:00","id":513039,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">There's a Background called Wealth that represented Underworld income (i.e., employed as a Reaper, a Byway bandit, Legion clerk, Bio-exorcist, etc.) that appeared in...either WtO First Edition or <i>Wraith Players Guide</i>. Can't remember which one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: <i>Wraith the Oblivion</i> (First Edition), p. 135.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","user":"Nazfool","date":". 05-13-2015, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}